// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  s7Signals.js — NC/PLC interface signals for SINUMERIK 840D.
//
//  GENERATED, then hand-verified. Do not edit rows by hand casually — regenerate
//  from the manual (see scripts). Pure data. Imports nothing.
//
//  SOURCE (every row):
//    SINUMERIK 840D sl — List Manual "NC variables and interface signals",
//    05/2017, A5E40870419, chapter 5 "Interface signals - detailed description".
//    Transcribed programmatically from the manual's own signal index; names and
//    directions are the manual's, not inferred. Signal flow (NC↔PLC) is taken
//    from each signal's "Signal flow" line where the manual states one; where it
//    does not, dir is null rather than guessed.
//
//  CONTROLS: tagged 840D sl AND 840D powerline — the DB10/11/18/19/21/31 NC/PLC
//    interface is common to the 840D platform. 828D uses a different interface
//    map (DB1200/1600/...) and is intentionally not populated from this manual.
//
//  RANGE RULE: DB31-61 are per-axis, DB21-30 per-channel. A class stores a db
//    range + offset, so DB34 resolves to "Axis 4" without 31 copies per signal.
//
//  EXCLUDED: tool-management DB71-74 signals use relative (n+k) addressing rather
//    than a fixed DBX byte.bit, so they do not fit an address lookup and are not
//    included here.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

